10. User Responsibility and Operational Risk

MyMole is a local storage-analysis, cleanup, and maintenance application. It
may inspect files and project footprints, retain scan history, move files to
the Trash, restore files, run external commands, uninstall applications, or
request administrator access for system maintenance selected by You.

External cleanup tools may permanently delete files instead of moving them
to the Trash. Files, caches, backups, project artifacts, settings, application
data, and system state may change between a preview and an operation.
Restoration and Undo may fail, including when the Trash has been emptied or
an original location is no longer available.

You are responsible for how You install, configure, run, modify, distribute,
and use MyMole; for the files, projects, applications, storage locations,
permissions, commands, and external tools You select; and for maintaining
appropriate backups.

Before approving an operation, You are responsible for reviewing its scope,
selected files, protection rules, permissions, and consequences, and for
ensuring that Your use is authorized, lawful, and suitable for Your systems.

The Licensor does not control Your files, systems, installed external tools,
or environment and does not assume operational responsibility for them.

